These Additional Terms are part of this license. They are strict
obligations and conditions on all your licenses, on the same footing
as every section above.

## Share Alike

If you distribute the software, or any changes or new works based on
the software, you must do all of the following:

1. License the whole of what you distribute under this license,
   this entire document unchanged, including every plain-text line
   beginning with `Required Notice:`. You may not add further
   restrictions and you may not offer it under different terms.

2. Provide the complete corresponding source code, in the form a
   developer would normally use to read and change the work.
   Distributing only minified, bundled, obfuscated, compiled, or
   otherwise processed output does not satisfy this condition.

3. Carry prominent notices stating that you changed the work and
   giving the date of your changes.

Running the software, including making it available to others over a
network, is not distribution and does not trigger this section.

## Grant Back

If you distribute or publish any changes or new works based on the
software, you grant the Original Licensor a perpetual, worldwide,
non-exclusive, irrevocable, royalty-free, fully paid-up copyright and
patent license to those changes and new works, with the right to
sublicense through multiple tiers, to use, reproduce, modify,
distribute, and otherwise exploit them for any purpose whatsoever,
including commercial purposes, under any license terms the Original
Licensor chooses.

You retain your own copyright in your changes. This section gives the
Original Licensor rights alongside yours; it does not take yours away
and does not assign your copyright.

The Share Alike section binds everyone else. This section does not bind
the Original Licensor, who is free to license the software and any
changes granted back under it on commercial terms.

## Commercial Licensing

This section grants no rights. Commercial use of the software is not
permitted under this license and requires a separate written license
